---
description: JStack per-role model choices (overrides skill defaults)
alwaysApply: true
---
# JStack model configuration, read by j-mode and the skills. One line per role. A comma in a role name means those roles share the line.
# Every role has a line. Any spawn without its own role uses `other helpers`. Never fall back to a model this file doesn't name.
# James Woods's choices: Anthropic leads every role and no OpenAI models are used. Gemini only takes a second seat beside an Anthropic agent that leads, on a panel or for a blue-sky take.
# A line gives the default, then when to step down or up, as `role: default; down <model> for <when>; up <model> for <when>`. Never start an Anthropic model on max, though escalating to max is fine.
# Load-bearing means hard to undo: data models and storage, public APIs, cross-service boundaries, and security.

# Jobs (see j-mode).
# Opus Medium: James's default lead (3 Nov). The lead (a Cursor Project chat, or an OpenCode lead session) plans and starts builders and reviewers, and the architect and reviewers carry the deeper reasoning. Cursor's Project settings set it; this line records it.
lead: claude-opus-5-5-medium
# Opus High: an ordinary design is cheap to change later. A load-bearing design is hard to undo, so deeper reasoning changes the outcome.
architect: claude-opus-5-5-high; up claude-opus-5-5-xhigh for a load-bearing design
# Opus Extra High: it runs only on a load-bearing plan, and its verdict gates every builder that follows.
plan reviewer: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh
# Opus Medium: James's default builder (27 Oct). The plan and the reviewer carry the judgment.
builder: claude-opus-5-5-medium; down claude-sonnet-5-5-high for very well-planned work; up claude-opus-5-5-high for a very complex change, or claude-opus-5-5-xhigh for the hardest pieces
builder for process work: claude-opus-5-5-medium; up claude-opus-5-5-high for harder pieces
# Opus High: one fresh agent per PR reviews hawkishly and fixes what it finds. High ties Extra High on CursorBench at about half the cost.
reviewer: claude-opus-5-5-high; down claude-opus-5-5-medium for small PRs; up claude-opus-5-5-xhigh for hard PRs
# Opus Extra High: it runs only on a stack with a one-way door, and its verdict gates the merge.
milestone reviewer: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh
holistic reviewer: claude-opus-5-5-high; down claude-opus-5-5-medium for a small stack
investigator: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
watcher: claude-sonnet-5-5-medium
# Opus High: prose and judgment calls inside a job.
judgment and prose: claude-opus-5-5-high

# Skills.
how explorer: claude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh
# Opus High: explains what the explorers already traced, with the code at hand.
how explainer: claude-opus-5-5-high
why investigators: claude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh
# Opus High: careful synthesis, but its answer informs James and gates nothing.
why synthesizer: claude-opus-5-5-high
reflect tooling: claude-sonnet-5-5-xhigh
# Opus High: James approves every proposed skill edit, so these seats don't make the final call.
reflect judgment, divergent, synthesizer: claude-opus-5-5-high
# Opus High: runners only produce candidates for the parent to pick from.
arena runners: claude-opus-5-5-high, gemini-4-carbon-medium
# Opus Extra High: the judge's verdict picks the base that later work builds on.
arena cross-judge pool: claude-opus-5-5-xhigh
swarm workers: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
# Opus High: runners produce candidate designs; the architect makes the call.
architect runners: claude-opus-5-5-high, gemini-4-carbon-medium
# Opus High: /interrogate runs only when James asks for it. Two model families catch more than more depth on one.
interrogate reviewers: claude-opus-5-5-high, gemini-4-carbon-medium
# Carbon Medium: an extra seat beside the leading agent, never the first agent. It runs when James asks, or a lead or architect judges a design stuck.
blue sky: gemini-4-carbon-medium; up gemini-4-carbon-high for a one-way door or when two fixes have failed
# Opus High: scans a decision trail for weak evidence and flags it. The flags are advice.
trail reviewer: claude-opus-5-5-high
comment sicko: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
other helpers: claude-sonnet-5-5-high
